  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">221997_FY24_UNICEF_Mozambique_Cholera Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cholera Response through RCCE and CATI interventions
 
 
 
 
 
 Key Objectives
 
 &amp;#8226; Affected population receive Case Area Targeted Interventions (CATIs) in response to Cholera
 
 &amp;#8226; Affected populations have safe and equitable access to, and use a sufficient quantity and quality of water to meet their drinking and domestic needs &amp;#8226; Affected populations have safe access to, and use appropriate sanitation facilities
 
 &amp;#8226; Strengthen subnational RCCE coordination structures, taking a multi-sectoral approach involving key government ministries, civil society organisations, traditional and religious leadership structures -
 
 Strengthen community health surveillance for case detection, follow-up and referrals to HCFs</narrative>
  </description>
